{"id":"m1-03-s3","title":"Stage 3: Chirp at 10k users","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: vertical vs horizontal, stateless app, L4 vs L7 load balancer, sessions sticky vs shared store vs JWT. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"load-and-goal","title":"Load and goal","html":"<p><strong>Stage 3: about 10,000 users.</strong> Goal: no single point of failure at the app tier and zero-downtime deploys. Capacity is still not the main issue; availability is.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 10k users, 30% DAU = 3,000 DAU. Each loads the timeline 20 times and posts 1.5 times, plus search/notification calls: say 30 requests per user a day = 90,000 requests a day = about 1 request/s average, peak 10x = about 10 requests/s. One <code>t3.medium</code> could still carry it. We go to two servers because (a) deploys and crashes must not cause downtime and (b) the product now matters: 10k users will notice a 5-minute outage.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 592.8 130\" width=\"592.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stage 3: two stateless app servers behind a load balancer\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M414.4 34 L470.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M414.4 34 L470.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M414.4 96 L470.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M414.4 96 L470.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M414.4 34 L470.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M414.4 34 L470.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M414.4 96 L470.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M414.4 96 L470.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Users</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ALB</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"359.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server A</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"359.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server B</text><rect x=\"470.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"525.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">RDS Postgres</text><rect x=\"470.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"525.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">S3 media</text></svg><figcaption>Stage 3: two stateless app servers behind a load balancer</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Netflix, Uber and Airbnb treat app servers as cattle: killed and replaced at will. Heroku popularised \"twelve-factor\" stateless processes.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A shop with two counters: one closes for lunch and customers just use the other.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"we scale because of load\" at 10 requests/s. The honest reason here is availability.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that the database is still one box.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"configuration","title":"Configuration","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>App servers</td>\n<td>2 x <code>t3.large</code> (2 vCPU, 8 GB), different AZs, Auto Scaling Group min 2, max 4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Load balancer</td>\n<td>AWS ALB (L7), idle timeout 60 s, HTTPS listener with ACM cert, HTTP to HTTPS redirect</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Health check</td>\n<td><code>GET /health</code>, interval 10 s, healthy threshold 2, unhealthy threshold 3, timeout 5 s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deregistration delay</td>\n<td>30 s (connection draining for deploys)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deploy</td>\n<td>Rolling: one instance at a time, wait for healthy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Database</td>\n<td>RDS <code>db.m6g.large</code> (2 vCPU, 8 GB), <strong>Multi-AZ on</strong>, 100 GB gp3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pool</td>\n<td>10 per instance x up to 4 = 40 (max_connections 200)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Media</td>\n<td>Moved to S3 bucket <code>chirp-media</code>, served via presigned URL for uploads; images read through the app origin for now</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Auth</td>\n<td>Branch 3C: JWT access token (15 min) + refresh token (30 days)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Autoscaling policy</td>\n<td>Target CPU 55%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>ALB target group health and ASG scale in <code>terraform</code>-style:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">target_group</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  protocol</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">HTTP</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  port</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">8080</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  health_check</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    path</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/health</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    interval</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">10</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    healthy_threshold</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    unhealthy_threshold</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  deregistration_delay</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">30</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">asg</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  min</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  max</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">4</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  target_cpu</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">55</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Health check that hits the DB: a DB blip marks every app server unhealthy and the LB drains the entire pool. Keep <code>/health</code> shallow; use a separate <code>/ready</code> for deep checks.</li>\n<li>Deregistration delay shorter than the longest request; users see 502s on deploy.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"decision-and-why","title":"Decision and why","html":"<p><strong>Decision 1: vertical or horizontal?</strong> Options: (a) go to a <code>t3.xlarge</code> (vertical), (b) two smaller servers (horizontal). Vertical is cheaper and simplest, but one box is still a single point of failure and restarts mean downtime. We choose horizontal for the app tier, and keep vertical for the DB (a bigger instance class is a trivial change; sharding is not).</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 2: stateless app.</strong> To run two copies, the app must not keep anything in its own memory or disk: no in-memory sessions, no local images, no local schedulers that would fire twice. Moves: media to S3, sessions out of memory (see branches), cron jobs to a single scheduler (ShedLock row in Postgres or an EventBridge schedule).</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 3: L4 vs L7 load balancer.</strong> Options: NLB (L4, TCP, millions of connections, microsecond overhead), ALB (L7, reads HTTP). We choose ALB because we want path routing (<code>/api</code> vs <code>/media</code>), TLS termination, WebSocket support and HTTP-level health checks; at 10 requests/s the extra cost does not matter.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 4: auth/session approach</strong>, detailed in the branches below.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 520 130\" width=\"520\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"L7 routing\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ALB</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"204\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"406\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">/api to App servers</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"204\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"406\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">/media to S3 or CDN later</text></svg><figcaption>L7 routing</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Netflix Zuul and Envoy do L7 routing; Facebook's Katran and Google's Maglev are L4 balancers placed in front of fleets. Cloudflare terminates TLS at the edge (L7).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> L4 is a post office sorting by the address on the envelope; L7 opens the letter to read the department.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"L7 is always better\". It costs more CPU per request and is overkill for raw TCP workloads.</li>\n<li>Not mentioning the LB is itself redundant: ALB spans multiple AZs by design.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"alternatives-branches","title":"Alternatives (branches)","html":"<h3>Branch 3A: sticky sessions</h3>\n<p>The load balancer sends a user to the same server using a cookie (<code>AWSALB</code> with duration 1 day). Sessions stay in server memory.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pros: zero code change, no extra service.</li>\n<li>Cons: uneven load (one popular user pinned), session lost when that server dies or deploys, autoscaling scale-in logs people out.</li>\n<li>Verdict: acceptable as a temporary measure only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Branch 3B: shared session store</h3>\n<p>Sessions in a shared store (Redis, 30 min sliding TTL, about 1 KB each). Every server reads <code>session:{id}</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pros: instant revocation (delete the key), small cookie, easy \"log out everywhere\".</li>\n<li>Cons: new component to run (ElastiCache <code>cache.t4g.small</code>, about $25 a month), one more network hop (about 0.5 ms), and it is a dependency: if Redis is down nobody can log in.</li>\n<li>Verdict: strong, and we will have Redis anyway in Stage 4.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Branch 3C: JWT (chosen)</h3>\n<p>A signed token carries <code>sub</code>, <code>exp</code>, and roles. The server verifies the signature with no lookup.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pros: no shared store, scales trivially, works across services later.</li>\n<li>Cons: cannot be revoked before expiry. Mitigation: short access token (15 min) + opaque refresh token (30 days) stored hashed in Postgres; revocation = delete refresh row. Use <code>RS256</code>/<code>EdDSA</code> with key rotation (<code>kid</code> header); never put secrets in the payload (it is only base64, not encrypted).</li>\n<li>Verdict: chosen for Stage 3 because no new infrastructure is needed; 15-minute revocation delay is acceptable for a social app.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Request:  Authorization: Bearer &#x3C;JWT 15 min></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Expired?  POST /auth/refresh {refresh_token}  -> new JWT  (Postgres lookup, rotated)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Logout:   DELETE refresh row  -> access valid at most 15 more minutes</span></span></code></pre>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>3A sticky</th>\n<th>3B shared store</th>\n<th>3C JWT</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Extra infra</td>\n<td>none</td>\n<td>Redis</td>\n<td>none</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Instant revoke</td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>no (15 min)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stateless app</td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Survives server loss</td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Per-request cost</td>\n<td>none</td>\n<td>Redis GET</td>\n<td>CPU signature check</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 607.2 130\" width=\"607.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"JWT verify has no network call\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M400 65 L456 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M400 65 L456 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M400 65 L456 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M400 65 L456 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ALB</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"352\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server</text><rect x=\"456\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"525.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Verify signature</text><rect x=\"456\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"525.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Postgres</text></svg><figcaption>JWT verify has no network call</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Auth0, Google ID tokens and AWS Cognito use JWT; Instagram web historically used session IDs in a store; GitHub uses opaque tokens. Many large systems mix: short JWT plus server-side refresh.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Sticky = same waiter always serves you. Shared store = a ticket number checked at the desk. JWT = a stamped wristband that any gate can verify.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Claiming JWTs are \"more secure\". They are more scalable; revocation is harder.</li>\n<li>Storing JWT in <code>localStorage</code> (XSS risk); use an httpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookie for web.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-breaks-next","title":"What breaks next","html":"<ol>\n<li><strong>Database reads dominate.</strong> Timelines are joins across <code>follows</code> and <code>posts</code>; as active users double, DB CPU climbs. Metric: RDS CPU above 60%, <code>pg_stat_statements</code> shows timeline query as top by total time.</li>\n<li><strong>Hot users</strong>: a post by a profile with 5k followers is read thousands of times, always the same data.</li>\n<li><strong>Images are served by the app</strong> through S3 reads: slow for users far from the region and wasteful bandwidth.</li>\n<li><strong>Failover is only for Multi-AZ</strong>; reads still hit the single primary.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 546.4 68\" width=\"546.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Next stage pressure\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M267.2 34 L323.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M267.2 34 L323.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Many reads</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">DB CPU high</text><rect x=\"323.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"211.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"428.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Cache + CDN + read replica</text></svg><figcaption>Next stage pressure</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Adding a third and fourth app server when the real limit is the DB. More app servers makes DB connections worse.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"cost","title":"Cost","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Monthly</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>2 x <code>t3.large</code></td>\n<td>about $120</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ALB</td>\n<td>about $25</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RDS <code>db.m6g.large</code> Multi-AZ</td>\n<td>about $210</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100 GB DB storage (Multi-AZ doubles)</td>\n<td>about $25</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>S3 + requests</td>\n<td>about $10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monitoring, logs</td>\n<td>about $20</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NAT gateway / data transfer</td>\n<td>about $45</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td><strong>about $455 per month</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>About $0.045 per user per month at 10k users.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignoring NAT gateway and cross-AZ transfer; they are a surprise line item.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"lld-view","title":"LLD view","html":"<p>Stateless service rules become explicit code boundaries.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>AuthFilter  -> verify JWT -> SecurityContext(userId)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Controller  -> Service -> Repository -> (Postgres)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>MediaStore interface -> S3MediaStore (replaces LocalDiskMediaStore)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>RefreshTokenRepository (hashed tokens, rotation)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>SchedulerLock (ShedLock): only one node runs each cron job</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Kotlin sketch:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> JwtAuthFilter</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">private</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> val</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> keys: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">KeySet</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) : </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">OncePerRequestFilter</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    override</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> fun</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> doFilterInternal</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(req: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">HttpServletRequest</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, res: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">HttpServletResponse</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, chain: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">FilterChain</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        val</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> token </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> req.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">getHeader</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Authorization\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)?.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">removePrefix</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Bearer \"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        val</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> claims </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> token?.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">let</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { keys.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">verify</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(it) }          </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// signature + exp check</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        if</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (claims </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">!=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> null</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) SecurityContextHolder.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">set</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">UserCtx</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(claims.subject.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">toLong</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">()))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">        chain.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">doFilter</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(req, res)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Statelessness checklist: no <code>static</code> mutable maps, no local file writes, no in-process scheduled jobs without a lock, config from env, logs to stdout.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 585.6 68\" width=\"585.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Request identity travels with the request\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M427.6 34 L483.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M427.6 34 L483.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Request</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">JwtAuthFilter</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"379.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Controller</text><rect x=\"483.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"528.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Service</text></svg><figcaption>Request identity travels with the request</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hidden state: in-memory rate limiter counters or caches per instance give inconsistent behaviour across servers.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"decision-gravity","title":"Decision gravity","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Decision</th>\n<th>Gravity</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Horizontal app tier</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Instances can be scaled back; it is just an ASG number</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ALB (L7) vs NLB</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>DNS cutover</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stateless design</td>\n<td><strong>One-way discipline</strong></td>\n<td>Re-adding state to servers later breaks scaling; treat as a permanent rule</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>JWT format and claims</td>\n<td>Semi one-way</td>\n<td>Mobile clients cache tokens; claim structure and signing algorithm need versioning (<code>kid</code>, <code>ver</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sticky sessions</td>\n<td>Reversible but leaves debt</td>\n<td>Easy to adopt, easy to forget</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>S3 for media</td>\n<td>Reversible if keys stored (not URLs)</td>\n<td>The Stage 1 rule pays off</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-AZ DB</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Toggle</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Treating JWT signing key rotation as a later problem. Put <code>kid</code> in from day one.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"concepts-learned","title":"Concepts learned","html":"<ul>\n<li>Vertical vs horizontal scaling and when each is right.</li>\n<li>Stateless services and the checklist of hidden state.</li>\n<li>L4 vs L7 load balancing, health checks, connection draining.</li>\n<li>Sticky sessions vs shared session store vs JWT (3A/3B/3C) with the revocation trade-off.</li>\n<li>Autoscaling by target tracking.</li>\n<li>Availability zones and Multi-AZ failover.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mixing up \"healthy per ALB\" with \"ready for traffic\". Use separate <code>/health</code> and <code>/ready</code>.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Stage 3 (about 10k users): 2 to 4 stateless <code>t3.large</code> servers behind an ALB, Multi-AZ RDS <code>db.m6g.large</code>; about $455 per month.</li>\n<li>The reason to scale out is availability and zero-downtime deploys, not raw load (about 10 requests/s peak).</li>\n<li>Sessions: 3A sticky, 3B Redis, 3C JWT; chosen 3C, with 15-min access token + 30-day rotating refresh token in Postgres.</li>\n<li>Media moved to S3; cron jobs are made single-run; the app now has no local state.</li>\n<li>Next bottleneck: DB read load from timelines and repeated reads, so Stage 4 adds cache, CDN and read replicas.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}